This extension adds Prey Vortex Extension (Alt version) modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

Now supports [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/prey2017/mods/103]Chairloader[/url] and mods that use it.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Prey Interface Customizer mods are recognised by a "preyinterfacecustomizergui.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Chairloader mods with a "chairmanager.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Chairloader mods with a "modinfo.xml" file install to the "Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Root Game Folder mods with a "GameSDK" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Binaries (Engine Injector) mods are recognised by a ".exe", ".dll", ".asi" or ".addon64" file.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Use mod type "Binaries (Engine Injector)" for upscalers, reshades, and other mods that should be in the same folder as the game's executable.[/*]
[*]Mods that contain a folder that is in the root game folder will be installed there automatically.[/*]
[*][b][color=#ffe599]Chairloader mods will be placed in the "Mods" folder (in the root game folder) automatically and kept in zips. You must then install the mod zips from the Chairloader GUI.[/color][/b][/*]
[*]For legacy mods you want to install with Chairloader, change the mod type to "Chairloader Legacy Mod". I did not turn on an automatic installer for this as it would interfere with users who do not use Chairloader.[/*]
[*]If your mod needs to be installed in another location, select "Root Game Folder" as the Mod Type and set up the proper folder structure for the mod manually in the staging folder. Looking at mods on the Nexus, there are a variety of different install locations represented, so please pay close attention to the installation instructions for each mod.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Prey Vortex Extension (Alt version) mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Prey Interface Customizer:

Recognised when the archive contains a "preyinterfacecustomizergui.exe" file.

========================================================================

Chairloader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "chairmanager.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Chair Mod Zip:

Recognised when the archive contains a "modinfo.xml" file.

  Installs to: "Mods"

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── GameSDK\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "GameSDK", "Whiplash", "Binaries", "Engine" or "Localization" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Binaries (Engine Injector):

Recognised when the archive contains a ".exe", ".dll", ".asi" or ".addon64" file.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
